+++ b/docs/bots.md
@@ -128,7 +128,7 @@ link unfurling, webhooks use the app's public-address policy to prevent requests
 to private/internal networks, with the resolved address pinned to the connection.
 The URL cannot contain userinfo or a fragment. Clearing the webhook, deactivating
 the bot, removing its room membership or mention, or deleting it/the message
-before the job runs cancels delivery. Network failures only produce a sanitized
+before the job runs cancels delivery. Network failures count toward suspension and produce a sanitized
 warning containing bot/message IDs and the exception class, not the URL or payload.
 
